# FitFlow Design System

Full reference: `docs/design-system.md`. This rule gives the essential rules every coding agent must follow.

## Stack
- **Tailwind CSS v4** with `@theme inline` — use `bg-primary`, `text-foreground`, etc.
- **shadcn/ui** components as the base — extend, don't rewrite.
- **OKLCH** color space throughout. Never hardcode hex/rgb/hsl.
- All tokens live in `src/app/globals.css`.

---

## Color Tokens — Required Usage

Always use semantic tokens, never brand tokens directly in components.

| Token | Use for |
|---|---|
| `bg-background` | Page / screen backgrounds |
| `bg-card` | Card surfaces, panels |
| `bg-primary` / `text-primary` | Primary CTAs, active nav, key highlights |
| `bg-secondary` | Chip backgrounds, subtle surfaces |
| `bg-muted` | Disabled states, empty area fills |
| `text-muted-foreground` | Captions, labels, secondary text |
| `bg-accent` / `text-accent` | Motivational highlights, streaks, energy |
| `text-destructive` | Errors, warnings, safety notices |
| `bg-brand-green-light` | Tinted success/completion surfaces |
| `bg-brand-coral-light` | Warm energy/accent surface tints |
| `bg-brand-sky-light` | Calm info surfaces |

**Never do:**
```tsx
// ❌ Hardcoded color
<div className="bg-[#22c55e] text-white">

// ❌ Direct brand token on interactive element
<Button className="bg-brand-coral">

// ✅ Correct
<Button className="bg-primary text-primary-foreground">
<div className="bg-brand-green-light text-primary">
```

---

## Typography Scale

Use Tailwind text utilities. Never set raw `font-size` in CSS.

| Class | Use |
|---|---|
| `text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight` | Page titles (H1) |
| `text-2xl font-semibold` | Section headings (H2) |
| `text-xl font-semibold` | Card headings (H3) |
| `text-base font-medium` | Body emphasis, labels |
| `text-sm text-muted-foreground` | Captions, hints, metadata |
| `text-xs` | Badges, micro-labels |

Line height: default `leading-snug` for headings, `leading-relaxed` for body copy.

---

## Spacing & Layout

- **Mobile-first**: Start at 375px. Use `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:` to scale up.
- Base grid unit: `4px` (Tailwind default). Always use multiples (`p-4`, `gap-6`, not `p-3.5`).
- Page padding: `px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8`
- Section spacing: `py-8 sm:py-12 lg:py-16`
- Card padding: `p-4 sm:p-6`
- Stack gap: `gap-3` for tight lists, `gap-4` for cards, `gap-6` for sections.

---

## Border Radius

Always use the radius token scale — never arbitrary values.

| Token | Value | Use |
|---|---|---|
| `rounded-sm` (`--radius-sm`) | 8px | Inline tags, chips |
| `rounded-lg` (`--radius-lg`) | 12px | Cards, inputs |
| `rounded-xl` (`--radius-xl`) | 16px | Large cards, drawers |
| `rounded-3xl` (`--radius-3xl`) | 24px | Bottom sheets, featured cards |
| `rounded-pill` (`--radius-pill`) | 9999px | Buttons (primary), avatars, badges |

---

## Component Patterns

### Buttons
```tsx
// Primary CTA — always pill, high contrast
<Button className="rounded-pill h-12 px-8 text-base font-semibold">
  Start Workout
</Button>

// Secondary — ghost or outlined pill
<Button variant="outline" className="rounded-pill h-12 px-6">
  View Plan
</Button>

// Icon button — square with rounded-xl
<Button variant="ghost" size="icon" className="rounded-xl h-11 w-11">
  <Icon />
</Button>
```

Minimum touch target: `min-h-[44px] min-w-[44px]`.

### Cards
```tsx
// Standard card
<div className="rounded-xl bg-card p-4 border border-border shadow-none">

// Featured / elevated card
<div className="rounded-3xl bg-primary p-6 text-primary-foreground">

// Tinted surface card
<div className="rounded-xl bg-brand-green-light p-4">
```

No `box-shadow` classes. Use `border border-border` for definition.

### Inputs
```tsx
<Input className="h-12 rounded-lg text-base" placeholder="..." />
```

### Chips / Tags
```tsx
// Selectable chip
<button className="rounded-pill h-9 px-4 text-sm font-medium bg-secondary text-secondary-foreground border border-border transition-colors hover:bg-primary hover:text-primary-foreground">
  3 days / week
</button>

// Active state
<button className="rounded-pill h-9 px-4 text-sm font-medium bg-primary text-primary-foreground">
  Selected
</button>
```

### Bottom Navigation (mobile)
```tsx
<nav className="fixed bottom-0 inset-x-0 pb-safe bg-card/95 backdrop-blur-md border-t border-border z-50">
  <div className="flex justify-around items-center h-16 px-2">
    {/* Nav items */}
  </div>
</nav>
```

### Skeleton Loaders
Always use `animate-pulse` with shape-matching containers. Never spinners for content.
```tsx
<div className="h-6 w-3/4 rounded-lg bg-muted animate-pulse" />
```

---

## Motion & Animation

- Use `transition-*` utilities for state changes. Duration: `duration-150` to `duration-300`.
- Prefer `ease-out` for entrances, `ease-in` for exits.
- Page transitions: subtle `opacity` + `translate-y-1` (never slide full-screen unless it's a bottom sheet).
- `tw-animate-css` is available — use `animate-fade-in`, `animate-slide-in-from-bottom` etc.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`: wrap complex animations in `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference)`.

---

## Mobile-First Rules

1. Default layout is single-column, full-width.
2. Tap targets: always `min-h-[44px]`, never smaller.
3. Use `pb-safe` / `pt-safe` on fixed elements near screen edges.
4. Bottom sheets > modals on mobile. Use `rounded-t-3xl` on drawers.
5. Avoid `hover:` as the only interaction signal — pair with `active:`.
6. Use `-webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent` (already set in base styles).
7. Test at 375px width first, then expand.
8. Sticky header height: `h-14` (56px). Account for this with `pt-14` on page content.
9. Bottom nav height: `h-16` (64px). Add `pb-16` or use `.bottom-nav-safe` utility.

---

## Icons
Use `lucide-react` exclusively. Size conventions:
- `size={16}` — inline in text, badges
- `size={20}` — buttons, nav items (default)
- `size={24}` — card headers, standalone actions
- `size={28}` — featured icons

Always pair icons with `aria-hidden` and a text label or `aria-label`.

---

## Accessibility Baseline
- Contrast: ≥ 4.5:1 for normal text, ≥ 3:1 for large text.
- All interactive elements: keyboard-navigable with visible `focus-visible` ring.
- Form inputs: always paired with a visible `<label>`.
- Images: meaningful `alt` text, decorative images `alt=""`.
- Use semantic HTML: `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<section>`, `<header>`, `<button>` (not `<div onClick>`).

---

## What NOT to Do

- ❌ `style={{ color: '#...' }}` — use token classes
- ❌ `className="shadow-lg"` — no box shadows; use borders
- ❌ Gradient backgrounds on text-heavy surfaces
- ❌ `z-[999]` arbitrary z-indices — use a clear z-index scale
- ❌ `overflow-hidden` that cuts off focus rings
- ❌ Placeholder text as a label substitute
- ❌ Multiple primary CTAs on one screen
